version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
keywords:
  - Mertens function
  - Mertens conjecture
  - Riemann zeta function
  - certified computation
  - ball arithmetic
abstract: >-
  A self-contained, independently checkable proof that lim sup M(x)/sqrt(x) > 2.0617536514585282 and
  lim inf M(x)/sqrt(x) < -2.0647155435291726, improving the bounds of Hurst (2018) on both sides. Since both bounds
  exceed 2, |M(x)| <= 2 sqrt(x) fails for arbitrarily large x. Ingham's theorem is applied at two explicit points; the
  finite sum over the first 14 400 zeta zeros is evaluated in ball arithmetic. Includes two verifiers based on different
  libraries and the zero data.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Hurst
        given-names: Greg
    title: "Computations of the Mertens function and improved bounds on the Mertens conjecture"
